<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Bruchhauser Steine circuit — Schmalah, reservoir, highest rock foot and northeast return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>This roughly 14.8 km Bruchhauser Steine forest circuit starts beside the B251 on the Schmalah approach. Follow the reservoir and shallow water crossing south to the turnaround, then head north past the paraglider launch to designated paths at the foot of Feldstein. Retrace those paths to the junction and return northeast to Schmalah. The secured summit ascent is optional and excluded. Confirm paid protected-ground admission, permitted visiting hours and restrictions before setting out; information-centre hours differ. Stay on designated paths, leash dogs and respect closures. No collecting, fires, overnight stays or wildlife disturbance is allowed. Only the separately permitted Feldstein stairs allow climbing; dogs cannot ascend. Use dry, snow-free daylight and non-slip footwear, preferably waterproof for the crossing. Paths can be rough, muddy or slippery and markings are incomplete. If the crossing or any required ground is unsafe, closed or unavailable, postpone the whole walk. The original 312 m ascent/descent and four-hour estimates are approximate; allow extra time. The map is for planning, not navigation.

Route geometry: Data source: Geobasis NRW, Bezirksregierung Köln, ATKIS Basis-DLM; Datenlizenz Deutschland–Zero2.0. Selected literal original walking features transformed from EPSG:25832 to WGS84. — Geobasis NRW ATKIS Basis-DLM original road and walking feature geometry — Datenlizenz Deutschland–Zero2.0. Licence: dl-de-zero-2.0 (https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/zero-2-0). Source: https://www.wfs.nrw.de/geobasis/wfs_nw_atkis-basis-dlm_aaa-modell-basiert?SERVICE=WFS&amp;VERSION=2.0.0&amp;REQUEST=GetFeature&amp;TYPENAMES=adv%3AAX_Fahrwegachse&amp;SRSNAME=urn%3Aogc%3Adef%3Acrs%3AEPSG%3A%3A25832&amp;BBOX=468249.1757121592%2C5682629.860978779%2C471099.93710936856%2C5687304.008776178%2Curn%3Aogc%3Adef%3Acrs%3AEPSG%3A%3A25832&amp;COUNT=5000. Dataset: https://www.bezreg-koeln.nrw.de/geobasis-nrw/produkte-und-dienste/landschaftsmodelle/aktuelle-landschaftsmodelle/digitales-basis.

